{
  "description": "A Python Client's hello accepted, a Run started and a page opened, then (ADR 0080): a click the Client cancels once sent, whose `$/cancel` the engine reads and answers with `call_cancelled`, and which the Client neither sends again nor undoes (ADRs 0080 and 0081); a finish with a timeout of 60 s that the Client cancels first, answered alike; a finish with a timeout of 2 ms that ends first, with `deadline_exceeded`, and is never cancelled; and the Run's finish. The `cancellation-reaches-the-engine` client conformance case.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "expect": {
        "method": "hello",
        "params": {
          "protocol_version": "0.1",
          "surface": "sdk_python",
          "needs": "collie",
          "product_version": "0.0.0",
          "form": "python",
          "log_level": "warn"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "reply": {
        "result": {
          "protocol_version": "0.1",
          "product": "collie",
          "product_version": "0.0.0",
          "engine_instance": "0123456789abcdef"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": {
        "method": "run.start",
        "params": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "reply": {
        "result": {
          "run_id": "01ke6p4ym0j8x3v5wq2rtbn7hc",
          "lifecycle": "running",
          "needs": "collie",
          "started_as": "new"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": {
        "method": "run.new_page",
        "params": {
